  "name": "Build Sales Automation for Every Lead, Deal and Renewal",
  "acrm---key-feature-1-content": "<h3>Every new lead assigned on arrival</h3><p>Demo requests, chat leads and event scans land in one table. Each new lead goes to a rep by territory or by round-robin rotation. The queue shows whose turn is next.</p>",
  "acrm---key-feature-6-content": "<h3>Territory rules stored as readable code</h3><p>Routing tables, cadences and the dashboard export to GitHub as code on paid plans. When a rep leaves, moving their accounts to a new owner is a prompt or a pull request.</p>",
  "awb---faq-data": "<div data-rt-embed-type='true'><div data-rt-embed-type='true'><script> window.awbFAQ = {\"heading\": \"Sales Automation Questions, Answered\", \"items\": [{\"q\": \"What is sales automation?\", \"a\": \"Sales automation is software that acts on events in a sales process: a form fill, a stage change, a date on a contract. Each event fires a step a rep would otherwise do by hand, like assigning the lead or sending the next email. Conversations with buyers stay with people.\"}, {\"q\": \"How do you set up sales process automation?\", \"a\": \"Write each rule as one sentence that says what happened and what should follow. For example, when a deal is marked Closed Won with an annual value over $50,000, open a handoff task for customer success. Give those sentences to Emergent's <a href='https://emergent.sh/ai-automation-builder'>AI automation builder</a> as a prompt, and it builds them into an app with its own database. Turn on one rule at a time.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is the difference between a CRM and sales force automation?\", \"a\": \"A CRM stores the record of each account and deal. Sales force automation works on that record: it assigns new leads and moves deals between stages when a condition is met. A CRM such as Pipedrive builds some of it in as trigger-and-action workflows. For keeping CRM fields current without manual entry, see CRM automation.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is the difference between sales automation and marketing automation?\", \"a\": \"Sales automation works on deals that reps own, assigning leads and chasing proposals that go quiet. Marketing automation takes on repeat marketing work, nurturing contacts by email and scoring leads by their behavior. The two meet at the handoff: once a lead scores high enough, it routes to a rep and the sales follow-up starts.\"}, {\"q\": \"What does sales force automation software do?\", \"a\": \"Sales force automation software keeps the pipeline structured. Every account has an owner and every deal has a stage. A stage change sets off the work that follows it, such as a task for the rep or a discount request for the manager. Forecasts then come from those stages, not from a spreadsheet each rep keeps.\"}, {\"q\": \"What are the best sales automation tools?\", \"a\": \"Salesforce Sales Cloud and HubSpot Sales Hub both include workflow automation. For a team already on one, that CRM is the first place to look. Outreach adds a sales engagement layer, with sequences that mix automatic emails and phone calls. When routing or approval rules fit none of them, Emergent builds that piece as an app beside the team's CRM.\"}, {\"q\": \"How does AI sales automation work?\", \"a\": \"AI sales automation adds a language model to rule-based steps. The model can draft a follow-up email from the deal record, or score an inbound lead on how likely it is to close. The rules still decide who owns the lead and when the next touch goes out.\"}, {\"q\": \"What is an automated sales funnel?\", \"a\": \"An automated sales funnel is the path from first contact to closed deal, with software moving each prospect to the next stage. A webinar signup starts a short email nurture. A click on the pricing link moves that lead into a rep's queue. To build the early, pre-sales stage on its own, start with a lead nurturing workflow.\"}, {\"q\": \"What are some sales automation examples?\", \"a\": \"Beyond lead routing, a team can rebook a no-show with a calendar link, or ask the rep for a loss reason when a deal closes lost. Contract terms outside the standard template can go through an approval workflow before anyone signs.\"}, {\"q\": \"How much does sales automation software cost?\", \"a\": \"The CRMs and the sales engagement platform compared on this page all price per user. A 15-rep team pays for 15 seats in whichever edition holds the automation it needs. An app built with Emergent runs on credits instead of rep seats. Emergent's free tier covers building and publishing.\"}]}; </script></div></div>",
